            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery disease in diabetic pregnancies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>150-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe vascular complications of diabetes mellitus include myocardial infarction and when this occurs during pregnancy it is associated with a high risk of maternal mortality. In the absence of myocardial infarction, information is unavailable on pregnancy outcome in diabetic patients with severe coronary artery disease or with prior coronary artery bypass graft. Such a case is presented together with a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
